      "id": "kv7qa8u",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background of Fundamental Duties"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Fundamental Duties were incorporated into Part IV-A of the Constitution under Article 51A by the 42nd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1976.",
        "The addition of Fundamental Duties was recommended by the Swaran Singh Committee in 1976.",
        "Originally 10 in number, the 11th duty was added by the 86th Constitutional Amendment Act in 2002.",
        "Fundamental Duties serve as a reminder to citizens of their national obligations and are non-justiciable in nature.",
        "Fundamental Duties apply exclusively to citizens of India and do not extend to foreigners."
      ],
      "id": "ut31375"
    },
