    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Fundamental Duties were NOT part of the original Constitution of India adopted in 1949.",
        "The Swaran Singh Committee originally recommended 8 Fundamental Duties, but 10 were added by the 42nd Amendment.",
        "The 11th Fundamental Duty (education for children aged 6–14 years) was introduced via the 86th Amendment Act, 2002.",
        "The Verma Committee (1999) identified legal provisions already existing for the enforcement of several Fundamental Duties."
      ],
      "id": "bnh5u84"
